<title>PARAGUAY: Paraguay 1996 inflation 8.2 pct, lowest in 15 yrs.</title>
<headline>Paraguay 1996 inflation 8.2 pct, lowest in 15 yrs.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguay's inflation was 8.2 percent in 1996, the lowest mark in 15 years, down from 10,5 percent in 1995, acording to preliminary Central Bank figures released Thursday.</p>
<p>December inflation was 0.3 percent, the same as November's but down from 0.8 percent in the same month 1995.</p>
<p>Wholesale prices were not released.</p>
<p>((-Jose Maria Amarilla, Asuncion Newsroom, 595 21 444527))</p>
